#Linux Commands Every DevOps Engineer MUST Know

If you work in Cloud or DevOps, Linux is non-negotiable.
Most production servers still run on Linux.

Here are must-know Linux commands 👇

🔹 File & Directory Management
ls | cd | pwd | cp | mv | rm

🔹 File Viewing & Editing
cat | less | head | tail -f | vi

🔹 Search & Filters (Very Important!)
grep | awk | sed | find

🔹 Permissions & Ownership
chmod | chown | umask

🔹 Process & System Monitoring
ps | top | htop | free | df -h

🔹 Networking & Troubleshooting
curl | wget | netstat | ss | ping

💡 In interviews, Linux questions separate real DevOps engineers from tool-based learners.
